+		 * is never a valid GC target block
+		 */
+		if (unlikely(!bdescs[i].bd_oblocknr))
+			return -EINVAL;
```
Reason:  
By rejecting any ioctl request with `bd_oblocknr == 0` at the start of each iteration, the dead‑block check will never compare against a zero original block number. This prevents the incorrect match when lookup fails, thus avoiding the subsequent call to `nilfs_bmap_mark()` on a non‑existent block.

